      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what we're working with.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Many unused imports\n- Unused helper methods (`doTestNoReplace`, `doTestReplace`) and an unused `values` field with its lifecycle methods\n- No comments explaining the six distinct scenarios being tested\n- Long, dense assertion lines with no visual separation between scenarios\n\nI'll write a clean, focused improved test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports, helper methods, and fields, then restructures the single test method with a named constant for the expected result and clear per-scenario comments that explain *why* each configuration behaves the way it does."
